Package: linuxcnc-status-agent
Version: @VERSION@
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.7), iproute2, systemd
Recommends: python3-yaml
Suggests: linuxcnc-uspace
Maintainer: Ajitesh Kannojia <aji.ajitesh1020@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/ajitesh1020/linuxcnc-status-monitor
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: LinuxCNC status monitor agent
 Streams live LinuxCNC machine state (cycle, parts, axes, spindle, errors)
 over UDP to a monitoring dashboard on the local network.
 .
 Runs automatically as a per-user service and attaches whenever LinuxCNC is
 running, however it is launched. Broadcasts on the LAN by default, so no
 static IP is needed. Read-only: it never commands the machine.
